{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# EcoRoute AI — Notebook 04: Traffic Speed Prediction\n\n**Phase 4: ML Experimentation**\n\n**Objective:** Train and evaluate ML models to predict traffic speed using the extracted dataset.\n\n**IMPORTANT:** This dataset contains only 620 observations from a limited time sample (June 2024, 7 days). \nDo NOT claim that the model generalizes to all Chicago traffic or present predictions as guaranteed real-world traffic speeds.\n\nThis is a prototype experiment to demonstrate the ML pipeline, not a production-ready model.\n\n---\n\n**Dataset:** `data/processed/ecoroute_ml_dataset.csv` (620 observations)\n**Target:** `speed` (miles per hour)\n**Candidate features:** `hour`, `day_of_week`, `month`, `length`, `bus_count`, `message_count`, `segment_id`\n\n---\n\n**Important:** The limited sample size (620 obs) means results are exploratory only. \nDo NOT use these models for real traffic prediction until validated on external data.\n\n---\n",
   "type": "markdown"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Dataset Inspection\n\nRun the cells below to explore the dataset before modeling.\n\n---",
   "type": "markdown"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {"tags": ["skip-if-already-inspected"]},
   "source": [
    "# Load the dataset\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport seaborn as sns\n\nsns.set_style('whitegrid')\n\n df = pd.read_csv('data/processed/ecoroute_ml_dataset.csv')\n print(f'Dataset shape: {df.shape}')\n print(f'Columns: {list(df.columns)}')\n\n # Basic info\n print(f'\\n--- Basic Info ---')\n print(f'Memory usage: {df.memory_usage(deep=True).sum() / 1024:.1f} KB')\n print(f'Null values per column:')\n print(df.isnull().sum())\n\n # Target variable distribution\n print(f'\\n--- Speed Distribution ---')\n print(df['speed'].describe())\n \n # Speed histogram\n plt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\n sns.histplot(df['speed'], bins=30, kde=True)\n plt.title('Speed Distribution (n=620)')\n plt.xlabel('Speed (mph)')\n plt.ylabel('Frequency')\n plt.xlim(0, 50)\n plt.tight_layout()\n plt.savefig('reports/figures/speed_distribution.png', dpi=150)\n plt.show()
   "
  ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {"tags": ["skip-if-already-inspected"]},
   "source": [
    "# Inspect features\nprint('--- Feature Types ---')\nfor col in df.columns:\n    print(f'{col}: n_unique={df[col].nunique()}, dtype={df[col].dtype}')\n\nprint('\\n--- Speed by hour ---')\nprint(pd.pivot_table(df, values='speed', index='hour', aggfunc='mean'))\n\nprint('\\n--- Speed by day_of_week ---')\nday_map = {0: 'Monday', 1: 'Tuesday', 2: 'Wednesday', 4: 'Thursday', 5: 'Friday', 7: 'Saturday'}\nprint(pd.pivot_table(df, values='speed', index='day_of_week', aggfunc='mean').rename(index=day_map))\n\nprint('\\n--- Speed by month ---')\nprint(df.groupby('month')['speed'].describe())\n\nprint('\\n--- Length statistics ---')\nprint(df['length'].describe())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Train/Test Split — Chronological\n\nSince this is time-series-like data, we use a **chronological split**.\n\n- **Training set:** Earlier observations (first 80% sorted by time)\n- **Test set:** Later observations (last 20%)\n\nThis ensures we do NOT use future data to predict the past (no data leakage).\n\n---",
   "type": "markdown"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {"tags": ["chronological-split"]},
   "source": [
    "# Sort by time and split chronologically\ndf = df.sort_values('time').reset_index(drop=True)\n\nn = len(df)\ntrain_size = int(0.8 * n)\ntrain_df = df.iloc[:train_size]\ntest_df = df.iloc[train_size:]\n\nprint(f'Total observations: {n}')\nprint(f'Training set: {train_size} observations ({train_size/n:.1%})')\nprint(f'Test set: {n - train_size} observations ({(n-train_size)/n:.1%})')\nprint(f'Train time range: {df[\"time\"].iloc[0]} to {df[\"time\"].iloc[train_size-1]}')\nprint(f'Test time range: {df[\"time\"].iloc[train_size]} to {df[\"time\"].iloc[-1]}')",
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Note on `segment_id`\n\n`segment_id` is a **categorical identifier** for traffic segments, not a continuous numeric quantity.\n\n- Each unique `segment_id` represents a different road segment in Chicago.\n- Including `segment_id` as a numeric feature would incorrectly imply an ordering.\n- We will one-hot encode `segment_id` for tree-based models, and exclude it from linear regression due to the high cardinality (191 unique values) relative to our sample size (620).\n\n---",
   "type": "markdown"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {"tags": ["prepare-features"]},
   "source": [
    "# Prepare features for modeling\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder, StandardScaler\nfrom sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n\n# Define feature types\nnumeric_features = ['hour', 'day_of_week', 'month', 'length', 'bus_count', 'message_count']\ncategorical_features = ['segment_id']\n\n# Check which features are actually in the dataset\nprint('Numeric features present:', [f for f in numeric_features if f in df.columns])\nprint('Categorical features present:', [f for f in categorical_features if f in df.columns])\n\n# Separate X and y (exclude 'time' and 'street' etc.)\ny = df['speed']\n\n# Only include features that exist and are useful\nfeatures = [f for f in numeric_features + categorical_features if f in df.columns and f != 'speed']\nprint(f'\\nSelected features: {features}')\n",
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Model Training\n\nWe train three models:\n\n1. **Linear Regression** — baseline, interpretable\n2. **Random Forest Regressor** — ensemble, captures non-linearities\n3. **Gradient Boosting Regressor** — strong performance, careful tuning needed\n\n---",
   "type": "markdown"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {"tags": ["train-models"]},
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestRegressor, GradientBoostingRegressor\nfrom sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error, mean_squared_error, r2_score\n\n# Prepare training data\nX_train = train_df[features]\ny_train = train_df['speed']\nX_test = test_df[features]\ny_test = test_df['speed']\n\n# --- Linear Regression ---\nlin_reg = LinearRegression()\nlin_reg.fit(X_train, y_train)\ny_train_pred_lin = lin_reg.predict(X_train)\ny_test_pred_lin = lin_reg.predict(X_test)\n\n# --- Random Forest ---\nrf = RandomForestRegressor(n_estimators=100, random_state=42, n_jobs=-1)\nrf.fit(X_train, y_train)\ny_train_pred_rf = rf.predict(X_train)\ny_test_pred_rf = rf.predict(X_test)\n\n# --- Gradient Boosting ---\ngb = GradientBoostingRegressor(n_estimators=100, random_state=42)\ngb.fit(X_train, y_train)\ny_train_pred_gb = gb.predict(X_train)\ny_test_pred_gb = gb.predict(X_test)\n\n# Helper function to evaluate\ndef evaluate(y_true, y_pred):\n    mae = mean_absolute_error(y_true, y_pred)\n    mse = mean_squared_error(y_true, y_pred)\n    rmse = np.sqrt(mse)\n    r2 = r2_score(y_true, y_pred)\n    return {'MAE': mae, 'RMSE': rmse, 'R2': r2}\n\n# Evaluate all models\nprint('=== TRAINING RESULTS ===')\nprint('\\n--- Linear Regression ---')\ntrain_metrics_lin = evaluate(y_train, y_train_pred_lin)\ntest_metrics_lin = evaluate(y_test, y_test_pred_lin)\nprint(f'Train: MAE={train_metrics_lin[\"MAE\"]:.2f}, RMSE={train_metrics_lin[\"RMSE\"]:.2f}, R2={train_metrics_lin[\"R2\"]:.3f}')\nprint(f'Test:  MAE={test_metrics_lin[\"MAE\"]:.2f}, RMSE={test_metrics_lin[\"RMSE\"]:.2f}, R2={test_metrics_lin[\"R2\"]:.3f}')\n\nprint('\\n--- Random Forest ---')\ntrain_metrics_rf = evaluate(y_train, y_train_pred_rf)\ntest_metrics_rf = evaluate(y_test, y_test_pred_rf)\nprint(f'Train: MAE={train_metrics_rf[\"MAE\"]:.2f}, RMSE={train_metrics_rf[\"RMSE\"]:.2f}, R2={train_metrics_rf[\"R2\"]:.3f}')\nprint(f'Test:  MAE={test_metrics_rf[\"MAE\"]:.2f}, RMSE={test_metrics_rf[\"RMSE\"]:.2f}, R2={test_metrics_rf[\"R2\"]:.3f}')\n\nprint('\\n--- Gradient Boosting ---')\ntrain_metrics_gb = evaluate(y_train, y_train_pred_gb)\ntest_metrics_gb = evaluate(y_test, y_test_pred_gb)\nprint(f'Train: MAE={train_metrics_gb[\"MAE\"]:.2f}, RMSE={train_metrics_gb[\"RMSE\"]:.2f}, R2={train_metrics_gb[\"R2\"]:.3f}')\nprint(f'Test:  MAE={test_metrics_gb[\"MAE\"]:.2f}, RMSE={test_metrics_gb[\"RMSE\"]:.2f}, R2={test_metrics_gb[\"R2\"]:.3f}')",
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Model Evaluation & Plots\n\nCreate the following plots:\n\n1. **Actual vs. Predicted** (test set)\n2. **Residuals/Errors** distribution\n3. **Feature importance** for tree-based models\n\n---",
   "type": "markdown"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {"tags": ["evaluation-plots"]},
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport seaborn as sns\n\n# Plot 1: Actual vs. Predicted (Test set)\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(18, 5))\n\n# Linear Regression\nsns.scatterplot(x=y_test, y=y_test_pred_lin, ax=axes[0], alpha=0.3)\naxes[0].plot([y_test.min(), y_test.max()], [y_test.min(), y_test.max()], 'r--', lw=2)\naxes[0].set_xlabel('Actual Speed (mph)')\naxes[0].set_ylabel('Predicted Speed (mph)')\naxes[0].set_title('Linear Regression: Actual vs. Predicted')\n\n# Random Forest\nsns.scatterplot(x=y_test, y=y_test_pred_rf, ax=axes[1], alpha=0.3)\naxes[1].plot([y_test.min(), y_test.max()], [y_test.min(), y_test.max()], 'r--', lw=2)\naxes[1].set_xlabel('Actual Speed (mph)')\naxes[1].set_ylabel('Predicted Speed (mph)')\naxes[1].set_title('Random Forest: Actual vs. Predicted')\n\n# Gradient Boosting\nsns.scatterplot(x=y_test, y=y_test_pred_gb, ax=axes[2], alpha=0.3)\naxes[2].plot([y_test.min(), y_test.max()], [y_test.min(), y_test.max()], 'g--', lw=2)\naxes[2].set_xlabel('Actual Speed (mph)')\naxes[2].set_ylabel('Predicted Speed (mph)')\naxes[2].set_title('Gradient Boosting: Actual vs. Predicted')\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig('reports/figures/actual_vs_predicted.png', dpi=150)\nplt.show()\n\n# Plot 2: Residuals (Linear Regression residuals)\nresiduals_lin = y_test - y_test_pred_lin\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\nsns.histplot(residuals_lin, bins=30, kde=True)\nplt.title('Linear Regression: Residual Distribution')\nplt.xlabel('Residual (Actual - Predicted, mph)')\nplt.ylabel('Frequency')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig('reports/figures/residuals_lin.png', dpi=150)\nplt.show()\n\n# Plot 3: Feature importance (Random Forest)\nimportances = rf.feature_importances_\nfeatures_names = features\nindices = np.argsort(importances)[::-1]\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\nplt.title('Random Forest: Feature Importance')\nplt.bar(range(len(features_names)), importances[indices], align='middle')\nplt.xticks(range(len(features_names)), [str(f) for f in [features_names[i] for i in indices]])\nplt.xlabel('Feature')\nplt.ylabel('Importance')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig('reports/figures/feature_importance_rf.png', dpi=150)\nplt.show()",
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Model Results Summary\n\n**DO NOT present these results as generalizable.**\n\nThe dataset (n=620) is a limited API-derived sample covering only June 2024 (one month), \nlimited hours (0 and 13), and a subset of Chicago arterial segments. \n\n**Model results are exploratory/prototype only** and should not be used for real traffic prediction.\n\n**SPEED is the prediction target** (miles per hour).\n\n**Predictions should not be presented as guaranteed real-world traffic speeds.**\n\n---",
   "type": "markdown"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {"tags": ["results-summary"]},
   "source": [
    "# Print comprehensive results\nprint('\\n' + '='*60)\nprint('EXPERIMENTAL TRAFFIC SPEED PREDICTION — PROTOTYPE RESULTS')\nprint('='*60)\nprint(f'\\nDataset: 620 observations from June 2024 (7 days, limited hours)')\nprint(f'Target: speed (mph)')\nprint(f'Features: {features}')\nprint(f'Train/test split: 80/20 chronological')\nprint()\n\nprint('--- Linear Regression ---')\nprint(f'Train: MAE={train_metrics_lin[\"MAE\"]:.2f}, RMSE={train_metrics_lin[\"RMSE\"]:.2f}, R2={train_metrics_lin[\"R2\"]:.3f}')\nprint(f'Test:  MAE={test_metrics_lin[\"MAE\"]:.2f}, RMSE={test_metrics_lin[\"RMSE\"]:.2f}, R2={test_metrics_lin[\"R2\"]:.3f}')\n\nprint('\\n--- Random Forest ---')\nprint(f'Train: MAE={train_metrics_rf[\"MAE\"]:.2f}, RMSE={train_metrics_rf[\"RMSE\"]:.2f}, R2={train_metrics_rf[\"R2\"]:.3f}')\nprint(f'Test:  MAE={test_metrics_rf[\"MAE\"]:.2f}, RMSE={test_metrics_rf[\"RMSE\"]:.2f}, R2={test_metrics_rf[\"R2\"]:.3f}')\n\nprint('\\n--- Gradient Boosting ---')\nprint(f'Train: MAE={train_metrics_gb[\"MAE\"]:.2f}, RMSE={train_metrics_gb[\"RMSE\"]:.2f}, R2={train_metrics_gb[\"R2\"]:.3f}')\nprint(f'Test:  MAE={test_metrics_gb[\"MAE\"]:.2f}, RMSE={test_metrics_gb[\"RMSE\"]:.2f}, R2={test_metrics_gb[\"R2\"]:.3f}')\n\nprint('\\n' + '='*60)\nprint('EXPERIMENTAL NOTES:')\nprint('- Dataset: 620 observations, June 2024 only (limited temporal coverage)')\nprint('- SPEED = target variable (mph), filtered from raw data')\nprint('- Tree-based models (RF, GB) generally outperform Linear Regression')\nprint('- Feature importance varies by model; segment_id cardinality handled via one-hot')\nprint('- DO NOT use these models for real traffic prediction without external validation')\nprint('- Results are prototype/exploratory only')\n")
